Guard Codex sessions against oversized catalogs

A simulated app-server cannot establish that real Codex emits a frame
large enough to break the remote session. Generate a local marketplace
with a 17 MiB plugin description and exercise the installed Codex binary
through a real pod and the remote TUI without inference or a live
catalog.

Verify the returned catalog exceeds 16 MiB, preserves its description,
and allows another RPC on the same connection. Require the TUI to
display the plugin through both production proxies. Restoring the
daemon's old 16 MiB frame limit reproduces the reconnect loop and fails
this test.
